{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Test leads and general heat shrink tubing fit my breadboard, relay, and wiring projects because they help me test connections and insulate the finished wiring.",
    "The caliper fits my need to check component sizes and mounting clearances, while magnet wire connects specifically to my past interest in ferrite toroid cores."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Filament assumes a 3D printing project that my history does not establish, and a feeler gauge addresses precise mechanical gaps I do not currently need to measure.",
    "The glues and epoxy require a bonding or repair task I do not currently have; buying fasteners and hardware does not mean I need permanent adhesives or ten containers of glue."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat general workshop supplies as interchangeable with the electronics supplies I have actually used.",
    "They assume that a plausible project connection is enough for a purchase, even when the material is specialized or the quantity exceeds my immediate needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more likely to choose something with a clear practical role in testing, wiring, or fitting components than something that requires imagining a new project.",
    "Related items can have different urgency: I would buy general tubing now, but wait on adhesive-lined tubing or a full spool of magnet wire until a specific task calls for them."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my electronics project interests but stretched them into workshop purchases without enough evidence of a current need."
}"}
